      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2781484923,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Why are we not just freeing the opt(ions) at the end?  Is it that much performance saving to remove once options is retrieved?",
          "author": {
            "id": 8399509,
            "username": "mmann78",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Michael Mann",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fad119898ba16a3f8be2f765dcff399098444abd4f85a04d4c3ef415a2bbe3d9?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/mmann78"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-09-26T14:14:19.272Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-10-01T08:28:40.784Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 418510023,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 6792385,
            "username": "AndersBroman",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "AndersBroman",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/132fb48f26018ea9516aea909144af3c3a94eaf2ba477efaa9a232abe80d322c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/AndersBroman"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2025-10-01T08:28:40.784Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 21475,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2782744876,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I would _guess_ that it is/was just a matter of convenience for `ex_opt_get_next` to remove the options as they are retrieved; This way the caller need not maintain any additional state when iterating (destructively) through the options.\n\nNone of the _current_ callers of `ex_opt_get_next` do any iteration anyway -- they only consume the first option in the list -- so there doesn't seem to be any real benefit the way things stand at the moment.  I _could_ just make the callers use `ex_opt_get_nth(\"read_format\", 0)` instead, and could then potentially remove `ex_opt_get_next` altogether (unless it's required for some public API).  Happy to take guidance on this. :smile:",
          "author": {
            "id": 7889756,
            "username": "dariusd0",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "dariusd0",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f0f4a609abaf984c9cfe277f1321b8db104aea7290fcbb7fb0c5749a00d32e39?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/dariusd0"
          },
